libSBML source code is NOT shipped inside this package.  tools/cmake_call.sh
downloads libSBML 5.21.0 from https://github.com/sbmlteam/libsbml at build
time, builds it as a static library and links it into the r2sbml shared
object.  The installed binary therefore contains libSBML code, even though
the package sources do not.

The build installs libSBML's own licence files alongside the library, at
src/libsbml-install/share/libsbml/LICENSE.txt (terms and copyright summary)
and src/libsbml-install/share/libsbml/COPYING.txt (the full LGPL 2.1 text).
Both are also available from https://sbml.org/software/libsbml/ and from the
libSBML source repository.

libSBML's main authors are Sarah M. Keating, Frank T. Bergmann,
Lucian P. Smith, Brett G. Olivier, Akiya Jouraku, Michael Hucka and
Ben Bornstein, with contributions from many others.

Note: libSBML also carries a copyright statement for the "SBML Layout" code,
(C) 2004-2008 by European Media Laboratories Research gGmbH (Heidelberg,
Germany).  That code is not compiled into r2sbml, because the build enables
no SBML Level 3 packages.  It would need to be listed here if
tools/cmake_call.sh were ever changed to enable them.


